          <div id="znid-009667354596"
            class="zn-element-wrapper 
                
              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>In Bethesda Game Studio’s hit video game “<a href="https://fallout.bethesda.net/en">Fallout 76</a>,” players are dropped into West Virginia decades after a nuclear disaster. The landscape is both eerie and familiar — its forests teeming with cryptids like Mothman and the Flatwoods Monster, its coal towns frozen in time, its hollers echoing with twangy John Denver covers. The game is an eerie love letter to the Mountain State, blending local folklore and real landmarks into a vision of apocalypse that still feels unmistakably Appalachian.</p></div>
