            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Long before she became the Mockingjay, Katniss Everdeen was a coal miner’s daughter from District 12 — which was once “a place called Appalachia” according to one of "<a href="https://www.suzannecollinsbooks.com/the_hunger_games_69765.htm">The Hunger Games</a>" prequels. The stories crafted by author Susan Collins are born of hard ground, where poverty and defiance grow side by side. The first film adaptation of the blockbuster book series brought that fictional world to life in North Carolina, with scenes filmed in DuPont State Recreational Forest, the North Fork Reservoir, and other locations around the state.</p></div>
